symbolic link is made from /dev/cdrom pointing to the actual device (if SCSI,
/dev/scd0). The /etc/fstab file may be trying to mount /dev/cdrom, which would
fail if no symbolic link is present.  That would also explain the error message
you have with bad device or partition number.

