Pat,

 By default it looks for /vmlinux.gz (you can set that in milo).  But the 
format, as far as I can tell, has to be a gziped kernel.  

  The best way to go about this is to do:
make config ; make dep ; make clean ; make boot ; make modules ; make 
modules_install.

When the make boot executes it will put a kernel in 
/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz that can just be copied to root and 
used.

Hope that helps,
Gerald

