Good points:
It's fast, and has a good warranty.

Bad points:
Pyxis chipset, doesn't run Linux (yet, I suspect Jay++ will pipe in with
some thoughts on this soon ;-} )
Has no cache in this configuration, no SCSI, ATAPI IDE CD-ROM, RAM expansion
is pricey, SDRAM is also rather dear. No SRM available yet, so DEC UNIX is
out. This will change over time, I imagine. By the time you have a decent
system with 2MB cache, SCSI, a useful root SCSI hard disk, etc... You will
be in for about $9000.

BTW, part number for this box is SN-B3AWW-EB
Different last 2 characters give different options, Replace the AWW with DWW
for 500MHz version ( not out quite yet, from what I see).

